{
  "about": "Cases both webhook receivers must answer alike: the Python one (src/klaxon/patient/services/receiver_app.py, run by tests/services/test_receiver_shared_cases.py) and the Go one (go/receiver, run by shared_cases_test.go). Each test fixes its clock at now, takes the secrets of secret_version (WEBHOOK_SECRET_VERSION) from secrets, sends the request to the receiver with a fake Kafka, up or down, and checks the status, the body, the headers named, the result counted in klaxon.webhooks.received (null: none), and the message written to Kafka (kafka_key: its key; null: none). A request is POST /webhooks/provider to the host testserver unless it says otherwise. body is sent as UTF-8; body_latin1 as Latin-1 bytes; body_repeat as text repeated; chunked, without a length. signature is the Klaxon-Signature header (none when absent); signature_latin1 is sent as Latin-1 bytes. signed_with says how the provider's signatures.sign made the signature; the Python test checks it. Made-up secrets, never real ones.",
  "now": 1791504000,
  "secrets": {
    "WEBHOOK_SECRET_V1": "shared-cases-v1-secret-not-real",
    "WEBHOOK_SECRET_V2": "shared-cases-v2-secret-not-real"
  },
  "kafka_headers": [
    "content-type",
    "received-at",
    "traceparent"
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a good signature",
      "secret_version": "v1",
      "kafka": "up",
      "request": {
        "body": "{\"id\":\"evt_000001\",\"type\":\"payment.succeeded\",\"created\":1791504000,\"data\":{\"payment_id\":\"pay_000001\",\"amount_cents\":1999,\"currency\":\"usd\",\"metadata\":{\"klaxon_payment_id\":\"pmt_000001\"}}}",
        "signature": "t=1791504000,v1=92874c035c149475861ca82b78d7f77cc83364d8551fbe514d325c932f543019",
        "signed_with": {
          "secret": "shared-cases-v1-secret-not-real",
          "timestamp": 1791504000
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "result": "queued",
        "kafka_key": "pay_000001",
        "status": 200,
        "body": "{\"received\":true,\"event_id\":\"evt_000001\"}",
        "headers": {
          "content-type": "application/json"
        }
      }
    },
